 {:seon.task/name "a-proof-of-what-moved-is-held-to-its-bound"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner, 2026-11-14 (on seon.render-cost-test/a-request-made-again-costs-what-moved): a proof named for what moved or changed states the lower bound of that work, O(what moved), constant in the whole's size, never the measured cost of today's design; a :growth :linear on such a proof accepts a design that re-walks the whole. [M] Sweep of test/ (web, 2026-11-14): eight cost proofs declare :growth :linear while their name or :work says what moved or changed: seon.problems-test/problems-move-at-the-cost-of-what-changed, seon.program-cost-test/an-update-holding-an-index-costs-what-moved, seon.program-cost-test/a-plan-reads-the-stored-reach-and-pays-for-what-moved, seon.render-cost-test/a-member-gone-costs-the-lists-lookups, seon.render-cost-test/a-step-costs-what-changed, seon.render-cost-test/what-moved-between-turns-costs-one-turn, seon.render-cost-test/a-request-made-again-costs-what-moved (bound worked: ~850 calls, ~1.8 MB, constant in turns), seon.render-cost-test/a-flush-costs-the-children-that-changed. PRIOR WORK: searched seon.cost (proof, :growth, steeper), seon.problems (the health classes over cost proofs), git grep 'what-moved\\|what-changed' test/ and resources/seon/tasks. Found: ```seon.problems/waived-proofs``` already walks every form that calls seon.cost/proof (one :form/refs seek, each form read once) and reads each proof map's estimate (:growth among it) for the :waived-proof class (docs/health.md#a-proof-that-passes-by-waiver). CHANGE: that one walk also yields a :moved-proof-grows row for a test whose name says what moved or changed (moved, changed) and whose proof map's :growth is :linear or steeper, so the rule is a health class, not a rule agents keep; then each of the eight states its bound as arithmetic (n, work per item, what moved) and the growth its bound says (:constant or :log), or its design gap is filed in its owner's namespace (each proof's area fixes its design). No second walk: the waived-proofs function becomes the one reader of cost-proof maps for both classes. COST: ideal, the forms that call seon.cost/proof read once, as today: n = 140 forms [M at root, result/b75393f9], ~150k ticks a form read, ~21M ticks and ~50 MB; the new class adds O(1) a proof map. MEASURED today: seon.problems/waived-proofs at root, 26.8M ticks, 51 MB, 3 rows [M result/b75393f9]. Owner: tests (the class); each proof's area its design."
